  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Lebanon continues to face a significant humanitarian and development challenge arising from widespread ExplosiveOrdnance (EO) contamination resulting from successive conflicts, sharply exacerbated by the 2024 conflict. EOcontamination continues to pose serious risks to civilian populations, restricts humanitarian access, delays safereturn and reconstruction, and undermines agricultural livelihoods and environmental recovery, particularly in SouthLebanon and other conflict-affected areas. At the</narrative>
